<tei:div corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:birkhot_haftarah/al_hatorah_shabbat"><tei:pb n="376" ed="1949 shabbat/shacharit/torah" facs="https://archive.org/download/PhilipBirnbaumHaSiddurHaShalemTheDailyPrayerBook1949/page/n400_medium.jpg"/><tei:p><tei:milestone unit="prayer-part" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:birkhot_haftarah/al_hatorah_shabbat/al"/>We thank thee for the Torah, for the worship, for the Prophets and for this Sabbath day, which thou hast given us, Lord our God, for holiness and rest, for glory and beauty. </tei:p><tei:p><tei:milestone unit="prayer-part" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:birkhot_haftarah/al_hatorah_shabbat/seal"/>We thank and bless thee, Lord our God, for all things; be thy name ever blessed by every living being. Blessed art thou, O Lord, who hallowest the Sabbath. <tei:milestone unit="prayer-part"/></tei:p></tei:div>
